	PROFHUB_OVERVIEW_HINT = "Treasures & Books: one-time KP treasures and books with waypoints. Course (101): the beginner course — chapters appear for your own professions. Weekly KP checklist: coming soon.",
	INFO_DRAWER_BODY_PROFHUB = "Everything profession-related in one place. Overview shows your professions, Knowledge Points and live tree advice; Treasures & Books tracks one-time KP pickups with waypoints; Course (101) is the beginner course.",
	PROFACAD_CH_KNOWLEDGE_TITLE = "What is Knowledge?",
	PROFACAD_CH_KNOWLEDGE_BODY = "Every crafting and gathering profession in Midnight has a specialization tree, and Knowledge Points (KP) are how you fill it. You earn KP from one-time sources (first crafts, hidden treasures, renown books) and from weekly activities — it is designed to build up over weeks, not days.\n\nCooking, Fishing and Archaeology have no trees and need no KP.\n\nDon't stress about being \"behind\": there is a catch-up system, and this course walks you through everything one step at a time.",
	PROFACAD_CH_KNOWLEDGE_TASK = "Open your profession window (default key: K) and have a look at the Specializations tab.",
	PROFACAD_CH_GEARUP_TITLE = "Gear up: tools, stations & first recipes",
	PROFACAD_CH_GEARUP_BODY = "First things first: the dropdown at the top of the profession window switches expansion tiers — everything in this course is about the MIDNIGHT tier. Don't see it in the list? Learn it from the Silvermoon trainers.\n\nEvery profession also has its own equipment — 1 tool and 2 accessories — in special slots at the top of the profession window (K). Without a tool equipped, many recipes simply won't craft. Most tools and accessories are crafted by OTHER professions (Blacksmithing, Leatherworking) — buy them on the Auction House under Profession Equipment, or ask a crafter; the supplies vendor sometimes stocks basics. Enchanting is special and crafts its own rods: buy the cheap base rod from the vendor, craft the Runed version at the Enchanter's Lectern (skill 1 trainer recipe), equip it.\n\nGreyed-out craft button? Read the requirement line in the recipe: it tells you whether you're missing a tool or need to stand at a station (anvil, lectern, cooking fire...). The stations are around the trainer district in Silvermoon.\n\nThen learn your first recipes at the trainer and craft them — skill 25 unlocks your specialization trees, and every first craft gives +1 KP.",
	PROFACAD_CH_GEARUP_TASK = "Equip a tool for each of your professions.",
	PROFACAD_CH_TREES_TITLE = "Choosing trees — without regret",
	PROFACAD_CH_TREES_BODY = "Knowledge Points are permanent: there is currently no way to refund or respec them. That sounds scary, but with a small plan you can't really go wrong.\n\nTrees unlock as your skill rises (the first around skill 25, more later). The classic pattern: pick ONE tree that matches your goal, fill its root node first (often ~30 points), then push one sub-branch (~20 points) before touching other trees.\n\nOnce you have professions, their starter chapters below give a concrete starter build — and MH shows live advice for your own trees right here.",
	PROFACAD_CH_TREES_TASK = "Look at your trees and decide on ONE first goal — don't spend anything yet.",
	PROFACAD_CH_RECIPES_TITLE = "Where do recipes come from?",
	PROFACAD_CH_RECIPES_BODY = "Recipes come from five places: your trainer (buy while leveling skill), your specialization trees (unlock as you spend KP), Moxie vendors (next chapter), renown rewards, and world drops or treasures.\n\nRule of thumb: craft every new recipe at least once. Each first craft gives +1 KP and 10x Moxie — even if you vendor the result.\n\nIf a guide mentions a recipe you don't have, check where it comes from before farming for it.",
	PROFACAD_CH_RECIPES_TASK = "Learn one new recipe and craft it once (first craft = +1 KP + Moxie).",
	PROFACAD_CH_MOXIE_TITLE = "Moxie, your shopping money",
	PROFACAD_CH_MOXIE_BODY = "Artisan's Moxie is a profession-specific currency: your Enchanting Moxie only buys Enchanting things. You earn roughly 5x Moxie per KP, and 10x from first crafts.\n\nSpend it at the profession vendors in Silvermoon on new recipes, bags of materials, and books that grant bonus KP.\n\nTip: don't hoard endlessly — early recipes and the KP books are the best value.",
	PROFACAD_CH_MOXIE_TASK = "Find your Moxie in the currency tab and check your balance.",
	PROFACAD_CH_WEEKLY_TITLE = "Your weekly routine",
	PROFACAD_CH_WEEKLY_BODY = "Most KP comes from repeatable weekly sources. The basics for every profession:\n\n1. Trainer weekly quest — unlocks after the intro quest at Captain Flaresworn (Work Order station, Silvermoon Bazaar). Enchanting needs skill 25 first.\n2. Two random treasure-drop items from open-world containers (+2 KP each).\n3. A Thalassian Treatise (+1 KP) — crafted by Inscription; warbound, so an alt or a work order gets you one.\n4. Darkmoon Faire week: +3 KP and +15 Moxie, monthly.\n\nMissed a week? The catch-up system slowly returns missed KP — after you finish the current weeklies.",
	PROFACAD_CH_WEEKLY_TASK = "Pick up the intro quest at Captain Flaresworn and do your first trainer weekly.",
	PROFACAD_CH_WORKORDERS_TITLE = "Work Orders (Crafting Orders) explained",
	PROFACAD_CH_WORKORDERS_BODY = "A Work Order (Crafting Order) is a 'made to order' request: someone wants an item crafted, and a player with that profession makes it. The Crafting Order table is in the Silvermoon Bazaar, near Captain Flaresworn.\n\nThere are four kinds:\n\n|cffffcc001. Patron Orders|r - placed by NPCs (no other player needed). YOU craft them for rewards: Moxie, recipes and Knowledge Points. This is the main weekly source of Knowledge for crafters - do the ones with a Knowledge icon every week.\n\n|cffffcc002. Public Orders|r - any player orders, any crafter can take it. The person ordering provides ALL the materials. As a crafter you can do up to 4 public orders per day, and you have 30 minutes to finish one after you pick it up.\n\n|cffffcc003. Personal Orders|r - aimed at one specific person (e.g. you ask a guildmate to craft for you). The crafter can add any missing materials themselves.\n\n|cffffcc004. Guild Orders|r - within your guild; works across realms.\n\n|cffffcc00How to BUY something made|r (you want an item but can't craft it): open the Crafting Order table, pick the item, and place a Public or Personal order. You usually provide the materials (plus a tip), and a crafter fills it - you can even ask for a minimum quality.\n\n|cffffcc00How to MAKE for others|r (earn gold): at the table, take a Public Order for a recipe you know, have the listed materials, craft it, and you get paid. You need the right profession, recipe and skill to fulfill an order.\n\n|cffffcc00Beginner tip|r: ignore Public/Personal/Guild at first. The one that matters early is Patron Orders - your weekly Knowledge engine.",
	PROFACAD_CH_WORKORDERS_TASK = "Visit the Crafting Order table in the Silvermoon Bazaar and open the Patron Orders tab.",
	PROFACAD_CH_ENCHANTING_TITLE = "Enchanting starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_ENCHANTING_BODY = "Enchanting is the odd one out: you earn most weekly KP by disenchanting gear. Each week the first 5 Swirling Arcane Essences give +1 KP each, then a Brimming Mana Shard gives +4 — that is +9 KP per week just for shattering loot. Enchanting gets no patron orders.\n\nStarter build (community consensus): Spellbound Shatterer first (its Shatter Essence buff boosts your crafting stats), then Elevating Equipment — root to ~30, then the Weapon/Ring/Chest branch (the most wanted enchants). Disenchanting Delegate is a strong third for material self-sufficiency.\n\nExtra KP books: Silvermoon Court renown 6, and the Abundance event vendor (Chel the Chip) sells an Enchanting book too.",
	PROFACAD_CH_ENCHANTING_TASK = "Disenchant gear until you have this week's 5 Essences + Mana Shard (+9 KP).",
	PROFACAD_CH_ALCHEMY_TITLE = "Alchemy starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_ALCHEMY_BODY = "Alchemy's trees unlock at skill 25/50/60/75: Potion Prowess (potions, Light/Void split), Fluent in Flasks (flasks, phials and a group cauldron), Transmutation Authority, and Alchemical Mastery.\n\nStarter build: put your first 20-30 KP in Fluent in Flasks or Potion Prowess — those recipes are what raiders and M+ runners buy all year. Transmutes and Mastery come later.\n\nDay one can be explosive: first crafts plus the one-time treasures are worth roughly 40-50 KP. Patron Orders (crafting order board) are your weekly KP engine — do them every week. The renown KP book sits at The Singularity renown 9.",
	PROFACAD_CH_ALCHEMY_TASK = "Do your available Patron Orders this week (crafting order board).",
	PROFACAD_CH_TAILORING_TITLE = "Tailoring starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_TAILORING_BODY = "Tailors are the only source of crafted cloth armor — and of the bolts (Arcanoweave and Sunfire Silk) that feed bags, embellished gear and spellthreads. Those bolts sit behind a daily cooldown that only specialized tailors unlock: reason enough to spec deliberately.\n\nStarter build: put your first ~30 points in the Nimble Needlework root (skill and stats for armor AND bolts), then pick your focus. Armor: Sin'dorei Finery — choose ONE slot group (e.g. robes/trousers/cloaks) and max it before starting another. Bolts/gold: Sunfire Silk Weaving or Arcanoweaving plus its Expertise node (more bolts, shorter cooldown).\n\nFiber Arts and Fabric Specialist improve every craft (and your cloth drops in specific zones) — solid filler for spare points.",
	PROFACAD_CH_TAILORING_TASK = "Unlock a bolt via Nimble Needlework and craft your bolt cooldown today.",
	PROFACAD_CH_LEATHERWORKING_TITLE = "Leatherworking starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_LEATHERWORKING_BODY = "Leatherworkers are the only source of BOTH crafted leather and mail gear — two separate trees, so pick one armor type first. Learned Leatherworker is the fundamentals tree and even lowers Concentration cost per craft.\n\nStarter build: Learned Leatherworker first, then Lasting Leather (leather) OR Safeguarding Scales (mail), maxing one slot sub-node at a time. Flawless Fortes comes later: profession tools on one side, consumables (armor kits, drums) on the other — those sell steadily.",
	PROFACAD_CH_LEATHERWORKING_TASK = "Choose leather or mail and max your first slot sub-node.",
	PROFACAD_CH_BLACKSMITHING_TITLE = "Blacksmithing starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_BLACKSMITHING_BODY = "Blacksmiths are the only source of crafted plate gear, plus weaponstones, tool stones and alloys. The Old Ways is your fundamentals tree (Ingenuity, Multicraft, Resourcefulness for ALL crafts) — feed it alongside whatever you pick.\n\nThen choose a focus: Armorsmithing (split by slot group) or Weaponsmithing (split by weapon type) — max ONE sub-node fully before starting another. Craftsmithing makes profession equipment for six other professions. Alloys, weaponstones and tool stones sell steadily without crafting orders.",
	PROFACAD_CH_BLACKSMITHING_TASK = "Pick your focus tree (Armorsmithing or Weaponsmithing) and max one sub-node first.",
	PROFACAD_CH_ENGINEERING_TITLE = "Engineering starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_ENGINEERING_BODY = "Engineers are the sole gun providers and craft goggles (engineer-only), bracers and boots — plus gadgets and scopes. Recycling is the fundamentals tree: skill on ALL crafts, and it returns materials while you work.\n\nAfter Recycling, pick one tree and max a single node first. Heads-up: in Bits and Bots the names mislead — Bits is reagents/cogwheels (scopes), Bots is optional reagents and gadgets. Scopes, boot attachments and gadgets are reliable auction house sellers.",
	PROFACAD_CH_ENGINEERING_TASK = "Put your first points in Recycling, then choose your focus tree.",
	PROFACAD_CH_INSCRIPTION_TITLE = "Inscription starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_INSCRIPTION_BODY = "Scribes craft staves, bows, off-hands, missives (stats on crafted gear), Vantus runes and Darkmoon cards. Unique perk: maxing the central Calm Hands node unlocks the weekly Thalassian Treatise — +2 KP every week, the only profession with that.\n\nSo: Calm Hands first, always. Then Blueprints (gear), Perfected Products (consumables) or Darkmoon Curiosity (cards, split by card type). Vantus runes, missives and inks sell steadily.",
	PROFACAD_CH_INSCRIPTION_TASK = "Work toward maxing the central Calm Hands node (weekly Treatise = +2 KP/week).",
	PROFACAD_CH_JEWELCRAFTING_TITLE = "Jewelcrafting starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_JEWELCRAFTING_BODY = "Jewelcrafters are the only source of crafted rings and necklaces — everyone needs those. Prospecting turns ore into gems; crushing turns spare gems into Gemdust. Tip: never spend Concentration on prospecting or crushing.\n\nStart with Thoughtful Throughput (fundamentals), then note two shortcuts: only the central Glamorous Gems node is needed to cut Eversong Diamonds at max quality, and Proficient Processor (prospecting/crushing) is cheap to complete. Cut gems and reagents like Sunglass Vial sell well.",
	PROFACAD_CH_JEWELCRAFTING_TASK = "Unlock the central Glamorous Gems node and cut your first quality gem.",
	PROFACAD_CH_HERBALISM_TITLE = "Herbalism starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_HERBALISM_BODY = "Every herb spawns in every zone, so no zone-picking stress. The big unlock is gathering while mounted: put your first ~40 points in the Botany root for that (Druids skip this — they already gather mounted — and go straight to Bountiful Harvests).\n\nThen ~40 in Bountiful Harvests (more herbs per node, more skill = more top quality), and after that per-herb bonuses on whatever sells best. Special infused herbs (Lightfused, Wild, Primal, Voidbound) can be Overloaded for a pile of motes — the first time per herb type even grants a Knowledge Point. The 12-hour cooldown drops ~30 minutes with every node you gather, and 40 root points add a second charge.",
	PROFACAD_CH_HERBALISM_TASK = "Unlock mounted gathering via the Botany root (skip as Druid).",
	PROFACAD_CH_MINING_TITLE = "Mining starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_MINING_BODY = "All ores appear in all zones. First goal: ~40 points in the Meticulous Mining root to mine while mounted — the biggest quality-of-life unlock in Midnight. Then ~50 in the Plentiful Ores root for skill on every ore.\n\nAfter that, fill individual ore nodes (spread evenly unless one ore is much pricier); maxing an ore boosts Dazzling Thorium drops from it. Special infused deposits (Lightfused, Wild, Primal, Voidbound) can be Overloaded for a pile of motes — first time per ore type grants a Knowledge Point. The 12-hour cooldown drops ~30 minutes with every node you mine, 40 root points add a second charge, and the Over-LODED tree buffs it further. Refulgent Copper is in constant demand.",
	PROFACAD_CH_MINING_TASK = "Unlock mounted mining via the Meticulous Mining root.",
	PROFACAD_CH_SKINNING_TITLE = "Skinning starter guide",
	PROFACAD_CH_SKINNING_BODY = "Skinners feed leatherworkers — and Midnight gives you tools for it: high-value beasts show on your minimap, Diffusers pull motes from mobs, and Majestic Lures (Talented Tracker) summon a once-per-day zone beast that drops epic materials.\n\nStarter build (farming): a few points in the Thorough Tanning root, then max the leather or scales branch, then back into the root. Next Gainful Gathering: Careful Carving (Finesse, mass farming) or Trophy Taker (Perception, rares). Swap tools to match: Finesse for volume, Perception for rares.",
	PROFACAD_CH_SKINNING_TASK = "Max the leather or scales branch in Thorough Tanning and skin with the matching tool.",
	TAB_DELVE_LOG = "Delve & Ritual Log",
	DELVELOG_SUBTITLE = "A per-character record of every Midnight delve and ritual run you finish: tier, time, deaths and (for delves) key used and the end boss. Tracked automatically — no need to keep this open.",
	DELVELOG_EMPTY = "No delve runs recorded yet. Finish a Midnight delve to start tracking.",
	DELVELOG_SEC_RITUALS = "Rituals",
