	PROFGUIDE_SUB_DAWNCREST = "Dawncrests",
	PROFGUIDE_SUB_PROFESSIONS = "Professions",
	PROFGUIDE_PANEL_INTRO = "Beginner-friendly profession help: what to do each week, where to spend Knowledge Points, crafting orders, and making gold on the Auction House.",
	PROFGUIDE_PICK_PROF = "Choose a profession:",
	PROFGUIDE_MORE_DETAIL = "More detail:",
	PROFGUIDE_BTN_WOWHEAD_PROF_FMT = "Wowhead: %s",
	PROFGUIDE_BTN_PROFESSIONS_TAB = "Professions tracker",
	PROFGUIDE_BTN_SMC = "SMC trainer",
	PROFGUIDE_BTN_WOWHEAD = "Wowhead guide",
	PROFGUIDE_URL_CHAT_FMT = "Link (copy from chat): %s",
	PROFGUIDE_URL_POPUP_TITLE = "Copy link",
	PROFGUIDE_URL_POPUP_HINT = "Click the box, then Ctrl+C to copy. Paste the link in your browser.",
	PROFGUIDE_BTN_OPEN_BROWSER = "Open in browser",

	PROFGUIDE_SEC_101_TITLE = "Professions 101 — start here",
	PROFGUIDE_SEC_101_BODY = "|cffffcc00Day 1 — do this today|r|n|n1. Press |cffffff00K|r (Professions) and make sure your two crafts are learned. Not yet? |cffffff00SMC tab|r in this addon → trainer waypoint.|n2. Craft every |cffffff00glowing new recipe|r once per profession (cheapest first).|n3. In Silvermoon: |cffffff00Crafting Orders|r table → Patron Orders that reward |cffffff00Knowledge|r.|n4. |cffffff00Professions tab|r here → map pins for treasures and books you still need.|n5. Enchant your |cffffff00weapon and rings|r.|n6. Below, pick |cffffff00Tailoring + Enchanting|r if that is your combo (plan for you, friends, and gold).|n|n|cffffcc00What is a profession?|r|nA profession is a job on your character. Some professions |cffffff00make|r items (crafting). Others |cffffff00gather|r materials in the world (herbs, ore, skins).|n|n|cffffcc00How many can I learn?|r|n|n• Each character can learn |cffffff002 crafting professions|r (example: Alchemy + Enchanting).|n• You can also learn |cffffff00gathering|r on the same character if you want (Herbalism, Mining, Skinning).|n• |cffffff00Cooking|r and |cffffff00Fishing|r are extra — anyone can learn them on top, like hobbies.|n• Many players use |cffffff00other alts|r in their Warband: one alt gathers, another crafts, and you send materials through the bank.|n|n|cffffcc00Knowledge Points (KP)|r|nKP are points for your |cffffff00specialization trees|r (like extra talents for that profession). More KP = better recipes and higher item quality.|n|n|cffffcc00Moxie|r|nMoxie is a currency |cffffff00per profession|r on that character. Alchemy Moxie only buys Alchemy stuff — it does not transfer to Enchanting. You earn some Moxie when you earn KP.|n|n|cffffcc00First craft bonus|r|nCraft every |cffffff00new|r recipe once if you can afford it. New recipes often glow in your list. Each first craft usually gives +1 KP (and Moxie). Pick cheap recipes first.|n|n|cffffcc00Your weekly loop|r (do this every week)|n|n1. Pick up the |cffffff00weekly quest|r from your trainer (often: finish about 3 crafting orders).|n2. Open the |cffffff00Crafting Orders|r table in Silvermoon.|n3. Do |cffffff00Patron Orders|r that reward |cffffff00Glimmer of … Knowledge|r (+2 KP) or |cffffff00Flicker|r (+1 KP, catch-up).|n4. Use the |cffffff00Professions|r tab in this addon to find one-time |cffffff00treasures|r and |cffffff00books|r on the map.|n5. Optional: Darkmoon Faire profession quest, treatise from the auction house.|n|n|cffffcc00Crafting orders — three kinds|r|n|n|cffffff00Patron|r — NPC jobs on the order board. Best for learning and steady KP.|n|cffffff00Public|r — Other players pay you to craft for them. Good for gold once you know a recipe.|n|cffffff00Personal|r — You craft for your own character only.|n|n|cffffcc00Specializations|r|nTrees unlock around skill |cffffff0025, 50, 60, and 75|r. Do not spread points everywhere at once. Pick one goal: |cffffff00flasks for raids|r, |cffffff00enchants to sell|r, |cffffff00leather gear|r, etc.|n|n|cffffcc00Gold on the Auction House|r|n|n• Focus on |cffffff001–2 products|r you can craft reliably — not twenty different items.|n• Check the AH |cffffff00before|r you craft a stack: price of materials vs finished item.|n• Raid flasks, weapon enchants, and ring enchants are classic sellers — but prices change every week.|n• Undercutting by 1 copper is normal; do not craft 200 items if nobody is buying.|n|n|cffffcc00Use this addon|r|n|n• |cffffff00Professions tab|r = live KP, weekly currencies, treasure/book pins.|n• |cffffff00SMC tab|r = trainers in Silvermoon.|n• Sections below = simple plans per profession.",

	PROFGUIDE_SEC_ALCHEMY_TITLE = "Alchemy",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_ALCHEMY = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (fast & cheap)|r|n• Trainer: Camberon in Silvermoon City; the supply vendor Melaris stands next to him (Sunglass Vials, Oil of Heartwood).|n• Pairs best with Herbalism so you farm your own herbs; otherwise buy from the Auction House.|n|n|cffffcc00Shopping list 1-50|r (cheapest quality is fine): ~300 Tranquility Bloom, 15 Sanguithorn, 12 Mote of Light, 4 Argentleaf, 4 Mote of Primal Energy, 3 Mana Lily, plus Sunglass Vials from Melaris.|n|n|cffffcc00The route|r|n• 1-7: craft 6x Silvermoon Health Potion.|n• 7-20: use Recycle Potions 10x on the potions you just made.|n• 20-27: at Camberon's Cauldron (next to the trainer) research Primal Philosopher's Stone + Lightfused Mana Potion, then first-craft the new recipes (each first craft = +1 Knowledge).|n• 25: your first specialization unlocks here.|n• 27-50: craft Entropic Extract, then more Silvermoon Health Potions.|n• 50-100: craft Light's Potential potions, or flasks if you have the flask spec, or transmutes - whatever is cheapest on your realm.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r: Camberon's Cauldron is a research object next to the trainer - it is not random. You pick what to unlock and pay some Moxie. Don't skip it.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_HERBALISM = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (by gathering)|r|n• Trainer: Botanist Nathera in Silvermoon City. Herbalism levels by picking herbs, not by crafting.|n• Start in Eversong Woods - easiest terrain and fewest mobs. Then visit the other zones for variety and first-gather Knowledge bonuses.|n|n|cffffcc00Skill ranges|r|n• 1-30: almost everything gives skill - pick whatever you find.|n• 30-60: the four base herbs (Sanguithorn, Azeroot, Argentleaf, Mana Lily) still give skill; Tranquility Bloom stops at 30.|n• 60-100: only Lush and Infused herb variants give skill - they spawn randomly in place of normal herbs, so just keep gathering.|n|n|cffffcc00Make it smooth|r|n• Drink Azeroot Tea (+Deftness) and Darkmoon Firewater - almost mandatory so mobs don't interrupt you while picking.|n• On your Sickle tool, aim for Finesse or Deftness; get enough Deftness to gather without fighting.|n|n|cffffcc00Infused herbs & Overloading|r|nGlowing herbs drop extra motes but hit you with a small debuff. After your first infused pick you learn Overload Infused Herb (find it in your General spellbook tab, not the profession one). 12h cooldown, reduced 30 min per herb you gather (~24 herbs to fully reset). Use it on Lightfused/Wild/Primal/Voidbound nodes for bonus motes - but skip Primal if you're below 50% HP (the channel can kill you).",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_ENCHANTING = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (fast & cheap)|r|n• Trainer: Dolothos in Silvermoon City; the supply vendor Lyna stands next to him (Enchanting Vellum, Refulgent Copper Rods). Disenchant any spare gear first - it gives skill up to 25.|n|n|cffffcc00Shopping list 1-62|r: ~412 Eversinging Dust, 27 Radiant Shard, 6 Mote of Light (you recover dust by disenchanting the rods, so you may need less).|n|n|cffffcc00The route|r|n• 1-25: craft 30x Runed Refulgent Copper Rod, then disenchant all 30 for skill.|n• 25-40: first-craft Enchant Helm - Rune of Avoidance, Thalassian Phoenix Oil, Enchant Ring - Nature's Wrath, then ~13 more Nature's Wrath, plus Flight of the Eagle and Hex of Leeching.|n• 40-52: craft 4x Thalassian Spellweaver's Wand (3 skill each).|n• 52-62: Amani Mastery rings plus a few helm/shoulder enchants; rush method spams Enchant Ring - Amani Mastery up to 70.|n• 62-100: craft one of every recipe you own, then whatever sells; Enchant Weapon - Worldsoul Aegis stays orange to 100 as a fallback.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r: Take the Gleeful Glamours detour - learn all 24 from Jennara Sunglow (tower behind the trainer) for +24 Knowledge. Pick a specialization around 60, not at the 25 unlock.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_TAILORING = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (fast & cheap)|r|n• Trainer: Galana in Silvermoon City; the supply vendor next to her sells Silverleaf Thread, Embroidery Floss and the Elegant Artisan recipes (for Artisan Tailor's Moxie).|n|n|cffffcc00Shopping list 1-50|r: 66 Bright Linen, 14 Eversinging Dust.|n|n|cffffcc00The route|r|n• 1-25: craft 66x Bright Linen Bolt - keep them all, you need them for later recipes even after they go grey.|n• 25-40: craft 14x Imbued Bright Linen Bolt.|n• 40-45: tick the \"First Craft Bonus\" filter and craft each remaining recipe once; equip the Bright Linen Tailoring Robe.|n• 44-50: craft 6x Courtly Shoulders.|n• 50-100: best done slowly - spend 5 points into Nimble Needlework to unlock a daily bolt CD (Sunfire Silk Bolt or Arcanoweave Bolt) and level off that. To rush: Bright Linen Spellthread (50-65), Sunfire Silk/Arcanoweave Lining (65-90), then Elegant Artisan items like the Cooking Hat (90-100).|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r: Your first specialization unlocks at skill 25. Tailoring is slow to reach guaranteed Gold quality, so there's little reason to rush - the daily-CD path also makes gold.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_LEATHERWORKING = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (fast & cheap)|r|n• Trainer: Talmar in Silvermoon City; the supply vendor next to him sells Silverleaf Thread.|n|n|cffffcc00Shopping list (through skill 60)|r: ~690 Void-Tempered Leather, ~610 Void-Tempered Scales, 3 Void-Tempered Hide, 2 Void-Tempered Plating, 4 Peerless Plumage, 3 Carving Canine, 4 Fantastic Fur, 10 Tranquility Bloom, 4 Mote of Light, 1 Mote of Pure Void, 75 Silverleaf Thread.|n|n|cffffcc00The route|r|n• 1-7: first-craft Smuggler's Leather Wristbands and Scout's Scaled Bracers, then return to the trainer.|n• 7-60: tick the \"First Craft Bonus\" filter, craft each recipe once, learn new trainer recipes every 5-10 skill, repeat through the skill-50 batch (~61); equip the Hideworker's Cover.|n• 60-91: craft ~35x of any one of Blessed Pango Charm, Primal Spore Binding, Blood Knight's Armor Kit, Forest Hunter's Armor Kit or Devouring Banding.|n• 91-100: keep going, or switch to any epic leather/mail armor recipe (3 skill each, only 3 crafts needed) via crafting orders.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r: Your first specialization unlocks at skill 25. If Fantastic Fur, Peerless Plumage or Carving Canine are pricey on the AH, just craft a different orange recipe that gives multiple skill points.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_BLACKSMITHING = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (fast & cheap)|r|n• Trainer: Bemarrin in Silvermoon City; the supply vendor next to him sells Luminant Flux, Blacksmith Hammer and the epic equipment recipes (for Artisan Blacksmith's Moxie). Pairs best with Mining so you farm your own ore.|n|n|cffffcc00Shopping list 1-50|r: 125 Refulgent Copper Ore, 100 Refulgent Copper Ingot (or 500 extra ore to smelt yourself), 6 Brilliant Silver Ore, 6 Umbral Tin Ore, 1 Duskshrouded Stone. For 50-70: 300 Brilliant Silver Ore plus 150 more ingots.|n|n|cffffcc00The route|r|n• 1-15: smelt 25x Refulgent Copper Ingot.|n• 15-50: tick the \"First Craft Bonus\" filter, craft each recipe once, learn new trainer recipes and repeat through all 28; equip the Thalassian Blacksmith's Toolbox and Hammer.|n• 50-70: craft 50x Sterling Alloy.|n• 70-100: rush with rare profession equipment via the Craftsmithing spec (1 skill each, no time-gated mats), or use epic equipment / crafting orders (3 skill each, ~10 to finish).|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r: Your first specialization unlocks at skill 25. The rare Sun-Blessed tools (Pickaxe, Hammer, Skinning Knife) are BoE, so you can sell the ones you make while leveling.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_ENGINEERING = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (fast & cheap)|r|n• Trainer: Danwe in Silvermoon City; the supply vendor next to him sells Malleable Wireframe, Pile of Junk, Arclight Spanner and Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor.|n|n|cffffcc00Shopping list (each trainer recipe once)|r: 145 Refulgent Copper Ore, 155 Umbral Tin Ore, 135 of one cheap recycle reagent (Powder Pigment, Refulgent Copper Ingot or Bright Linen Bolt), 21 Malleable Wireframe, 35 Pile of Junk, plus 1 each of Mote of Light/Primal Energy/Wild Magic/Pure Void.|n|n|cffffcc00The route|r|n• 1-16: craft 8x Song Gear, then 7x Recycling.|n• 16-39: first-craft the Evercore items (Shade, Vision Guard, Dome Dinger, Zoomshroud, Reconissance), pick Recycling as your first spec, then craft 10x Soul Sprocket and the four Cogwheels.|n• 39-45: 20x Recycling, then first-craft each new bonus recipe.|n• 45-80: Recycle until you discover a Quel'dorei recipe, then mass-craft Quel'dorei gear (e.g. 60x Quel'dorei Guards).|n• 80-100: craft Housing Decor (the only non-order path to 100), rare equipment, or epic tools/armor via crafting orders.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r: Recycling discovery is locked by default - put 10 points into the Recycling spec first or the cheap Quel'dorei recipes never appear. The points aren't wasted; they add crafting skill too.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_INSCRIPTION = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (fast & cheap)|r|n• Trainer: Zantasia in Silvermoon City; the supply vendor near her sells Thalassian Songwater and Lexicologist's Vellum.|n|n|cffffcc00Shopping list 1-100|r: 360 Tranquility Bloom, 100 Argentleaf, 90 Mana Lily, 90 Sanguithorn, 65 Azeroot, 1 Duskshrouded Stone, 1 Mote of Light, 4 Mote of Primal Energy, 7 Mote of Wild Magic, 4 Mote of Pure Void.|n|n|cffffcc00The route|r|n• 1-20: use Midnight Milling on all your herbs.|n• 20-30: craft 11x Munsell Ink then 12x Sienna Ink - keep them. At 25 learn Calm Hands as your first spec (it teaches the Treatise recipe).|n• 30-45: first-craft the batons, Soul Cipher and Missives via the \"First Craft Bonus\" filter, then up to 3x Thalassian Treatise on Inscription.|n• 45-100: keep crafting Thalassian Treatise on Inscription (~70 total) - you discover Treatises for the other professions as you go, so first-craft each for bonus skill.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r: Buying inks straight from the Auction House is usually faster and cheaper than milling pigments. Don't use the Treatise consumable until you've decided your spec - 10 points in Calm Hands turns it into 2 Knowledge.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_JEWELCRAFTING = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (fast & cheap)|r|n• Trainer: Amin in Silvermoon City; the supply vendor next to him sells the Jeweler's Toolset. Pairs best with Mining so you farm your own ore and gems.|n|n|cffffcc00Shopping list (each trainer recipe once)|r: 60 cheap ore (Refulgent Copper/Umbral Tin/Brilliant Silver), 31 Glimmering Gemdust, 100 Crystalline Glass, 7 Duskshrouded Stone, 5 Sanguine Garnet, 4 each of Tenebrous Amethyst/Harandar Peridot/Amani Lapis, plus one Flawless of each gem.|n|n|cffffcc00The route|r|n• 1-14: 12x Midnight Prospecting, then craft 4x Sin'dorei Lens.|n• 14-50: tick the \"First Craft Bonus\" filter and craft each trainer recipe once, learning new ones every 5 skill.|n• 50-65: craft 40x Monologuer's Chalice (very cheap).|n• 65-100 (optional): cut Eversong Diamonds (2 skill each), spam rare/epic profession equipment from Gelanthis, or fill jewelry crafting orders if specced for rings/necklaces.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r: Your first specialization unlocks at skill 25. Keep the trainer and your profession window open side by side for the 14-50 stretch - new recipes arrive every 5 skill and one first-craft each keeps you on pace.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_MINING = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (by gathering)|r|n• Trainer: Belil in Silvermoon City. Mining levels by mining deposit nodes, not by crafting.|n• Start in Eversong Woods - easiest terrain and lowest mob density. Then visit Zul'Aman, Harandar and Voidstorm for variety and first-gather Knowledge.|n|n|cffffcc00Skill ranges|r|n• 1-30: almost every deposit gives skill - mine whatever you find.|n• 30-60: base deposits go yellow at 30; Rich deposits, Seams and Infused variants still give skill.|n• 60-100: base deposits are grey - only Rich deposits, Seams and Infused variants give skill, spawning randomly in place of normal ones.|n|n|cffffcc00Make it smooth|r|n• Drink Azeroot Tea (+Deftness) and Darkmoon Firewater - nodes take a while to channel, so this is basically mandatory.|n• On your Pickaxe, aim for Deftness or Finesse; get enough Deftness to mine without fighting.|n|n|cffffcc00Infused deposits & Overloading|r|nGlowing deposits drop extra motes but apply a debuff. Your first Infused mine teaches Overload (General spellbook tab, not the profession one). 12h cooldown, reduced 30 min per deposit mined (~24 to fully reset). Use it on Lightfused/Wild/Primal/Voidbound nodes - but skip Primal below 50% HP (the channel can kill you) and don't waste it on Zul'Aman's Wild deposits.",
	PROFGUIDE_LVL_SKINNING = "|cffffcc00Skill leveling 1-100 (by gathering)|r|n• Trainer: Tyn in Silvermoon City. Skinning levels by skinning beasts, not by crafting.|n• Farm Void-Tempered Leather from leather mobs and Void-Tempered Scales in Eversong Woods (Agitated Wyrms, Territorial Dragonhawks); fur, plumage and fangs come from the matching creatures.|n|n|cffffcc00How it works|r|nThere is no Classic-style numeric table - skinning skill scales through the specialization trees, fuelled by Knowledge Points. Three trees: Thorough Tanning (more leather/scales), Gainful Gathering (motes & unique mats) and Talented Tracker (lures & Renowned Beasts).|n|n|cffffcc00Pure farming build|r|n• 0-80 points: 10 into Thorough Tanning, then Lasting Leather or Superb Scales (40), then 30 back into Thorough Tanning.|n• 80-130 points: 10 into Gainful Gathering, then Careful Carving or Trophy Taker (40).|n|n|cffffcc00Tips|r|n• High Value Beasts show a glowing skinning-knife icon on the minimap and yield 5-10 extra hides - tracking is on by default.|n• Carry two knives: Finesse for more base materials, Perception for an extra roll on rares - swap to Perception when using Sharpen Your Knife or skinning Renowned Beasts. Match your consumables (Argentleaf Tea / Sanguithorn Tea) to the knife.",
	PROFGUIDE_SEC_ALCHEMY_BODY = "|cffffcc00What it does|r|nTurns herbs into |cffffff00potions|r (short buffs) and |cffffff00flasks|r (long buffs for raids). Great for |cffffff00yourself|r and for |cffffff00gold|r.|n|n|cffffcc00Good combo|r|nLearn |cffffff00Herbalism|r on this character or on a gather-alt and send herbs through the Warband bank.|n|n|cffffcc00Week 1 checklist|r|n|n• Learn Alchemy in Silvermoon.|n• Craft every cheap |cffffff00new recipe|r once (first-craft KP).|n• Finish the |cffffff00weekly trainer quest|r (usually 3 orders).|n• Do Patron Orders with |cffffff00Glimmer of Alchemy Knowledge|r.|n• Pick one path: |cffffff00flasks|r OR |cffffff00potions|r — not both at the start.|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP — for yourself|r|n|n• Put early points into the specialization that unlocks |cffffff00flasks your raid uses|r.|n• Ask your guild or check the AH: which flask sells most this tier?|n• Quality matters: higher quality flask = stronger buff. Use |cffffff00Concentration|r on important crafts (the game shows this on the craft screen).|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP — for gold|r|n|n• Same idea: one |cffffff00popular raid flask|r per season.|n• Watch material cost vs flask price for a week before you commit.|n• Do not craft 50 flasks if the AH is already flooded.|n|n|cffffcc00Crafting orders|r|nPatron orders are your best friend. Public orders can pay well once your skill is high enough for |cffffff00Quality 2–3|r.|n|n|cffffcc00Auction House|r|nSell |cffffff00flasks|r before raid nights (Tuesday/Wednesday on many realms). Potions can sell too but often in smaller amounts.",

	PROFGUIDE_SEC_COMBO_TE_TITLE = "Tailoring + Enchanting",
	PROFGUIDE_SEC_COMBO_TE_BODY = "|cffffcc00Your combo|r|n|cffffff00Tailoring|r makes cloth gear and extras. |cffffff00Enchanting|r makes gear stronger — great for |cffffff00yourself|r, |cffffff00friends and guild|r, and |cffffff00gold|r on the Auction House.|n|n|cffffcc00Day 1–3 (in order)|r|n|n1. Learn both in Silvermoon (|cffffff00SMC tab|r → Enchanting + Tailoring trainers).|n2. First-craft cheap recipes on |cffffff00both|r professions.|n3. Pick up the |cffffff00weekly quest|r at each trainer (often ~3 orders each).|n4. Crafting Orders board: Patron Orders with |cffffff00Glimmer of … Knowledge|r — do some on Enchanting, some on Tailoring.|n5. |cffffff00Professions tab|r in this addon: treasures and books for |cffffff00both|r.|n|n|cffffcc00For yourself|r|n|n• Enchant: |cffffff00weapon|r, then |cffffff00rings|r, then bracers, boots, cloak.|n• Tailoring: craft cloth pieces for slots you actually wear.|n• Each profession has its own KP — Enchanting KP only spends in Enchanting, Tailoring KP only in Tailoring.|n|n|cffffcc00For friends, partner, guild|r|n|n• Before content: ask \"need a weapon or ring enchant?\" They bring the item or buy vellum.|n• Keep 2–3 enchants you can always craft without looking everything up.|n• Cloth friends: offer bracers or cloak upgrades if you have a good recipe — they bring cloth or tip you.|n• Only disenchant |cffffff00your own|r junk gear unless they ask you to DE something.|n|n|cffffcc00For gold|r|n|n• |cffffff00Ring and weapon enchants|r on the AH — check prices before you craft a big stack.|n• |cffffff00Public orders|r in Silvermoon for popular enchants when your quality is high enough.|n• Tailoring: sometimes |cffffff00bags|r or hot cloth pieces sell — peek at the AH one evening.|n• Buy cloth only when the math works (finished item price higher than cloth cost).|n|n|cffffcc00Every week (both)|r|n|n1. Two weekly trainer quests.|n2. Patron Orders with Knowledge on both boards.|n3. A few new first-crafts if you learned recipes.|n4. Disenchant greens you loot for enchanting mats.|n5. One AH check: which enchant or cloth item is worth crafting.|n|n|cffffcc00Mistakes to avoid|r|n|n• Ignoring Enchanting for weeks — separate KP and weekly quests from Tailoring.|n• Dumping all Tailoring KP into one branch that does not help gear you wear.|n• Crafting random tailoring nobody buys.|n• Skipping Patron Orders on either profession — steady KP on each.",

	PROFGUIDE_SEC_ENCHANTING_TITLE = "Enchanting",
	PROFGUIDE_SEC_ENCHANTING_BODY = "|cffffcc00What it does|r|nPuts |cffffff00enchants|r on weapons and armor. You also |cffffff00disenchant|r old gear into dust and shards.|n|n|cffffcc00Week 1 checklist|r|n|n• Learn Enchanting in Silvermoon.|n• Disenchant |cffffff00green and blue|r gear you do not need (steady KP while leveling).|n• First-craft every cheap formula once.|n• Weekly quest + Patron Orders with Knowledge rewards.|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP — for yourself|r|n|n• Early: points that help you |cffffff00disenchant|r and craft basic materials.|n• Then: enchants for |cffffff00your own gear slots|r (weapon first, then ring/bracers).|n|n|cffffcc00For friends and guild|r|n|n• Offer weapon and ring enchants before dungeons or raid.|n• They trade you the item, or you craft onto vellum they bought.|n• Write down 2–3 \"house enchants\" you always have ready.|n• With Tailoring on the same character: you cover enchants, they bring cloth if you craft for them.|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP — for gold|r|n|n• |cffffff00Ring enchants|r and |cffffff00weapon enchants|r are always in demand.|n• Pick |cffffff00one|r market (weapons OR rings) so you do not run out of KP.|n• Post enchants on the AH as items — players buy the vellum/enchant and apply it themselves.|n|n|cffffcc00Crafting orders|r|nPublic orders for popular enchants can be good gold. Patron orders still matter for KP every week.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r|nKeep a bag of unneeded greens from world quests and delves — disenchant them instead of vendoring.",

	PROFGUIDE_SEC_TAILORING_TITLE = "Tailoring",
	PROFGUIDE_SEC_TAILORING_BODY = "|cffffcc00What it does|r|nTurns |cffffff00cloth|r (from the Auction House or vendors) into cloth armor, bags, and other items. Pairs perfectly with |cffffff00Enchanting|r on the same character.|n|n|cffffcc00Week 1 checklist|r|n|n• Learn Tailoring in Silvermoon.|n• Buy a little cloth or farm while questing — do not overbuy on day one.|n• First-craft every cheap |cffffff00new recipe|r once.|n• Weekly quest + Patron Orders with Knowledge rewards.|n• Craft upgrades for slots you |cffffff00actually wear|r (cloth users: Mage, Priest, Warlock, Evoker, etc.).|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP — for yourself|r|n|n• Points into the armor type you wear.|n• Bags and utility are nice, but armor power usually comes first.|n• Then enchant those pieces with Enchanting.|n|n|cffffcc00For friends and guild|r|n|n• Offer bracers, cloak, or belt crafts if you have a good recipe.|n• They provide cloth or pay a tip — agree before you craft.|n• You are not a full gear vendor yet; start with close friends.|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP — for gold|r|n|n• Watch the AH: sometimes |cffffff00bags|r or popular cloth slots sell.|n• Only craft when |cffffff00sell price|r beats |cffffff00cloth cost|r.|n• Public tailoring orders in Silvermoon can pay once your quality is higher.|n|n|cffffcc00With Enchanting|r|nYou make the item; Enchanting makes it strong. That is why this duo is popular for yourself and for helping others.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r|nCloth is not gathered on this character — check cloth prices on the AH before you commit to a big craft.",

	PROFGUIDE_SEC_HERBALISM_TITLE = "Herbalism",
	PROFGUIDE_SEC_HERBALISM_BODY = "|cffffcc00What it does|r|nYou |cffffff00pick herbs|r in the world. Herbs feed |cffffff00Alchemy|r and some other crafts.|n|n|cffffcc00Who should learn it?|r|n|n• Anyone who wants to |cffffff00save gold|r on potions/flasks.|n• Often on a |cffffff00second character|r while your main does Alchemy.|n|n|cffffcc00Week 1 checklist|r|n|n• Learn Herbalism — no crafting orders needed for the weekly loop like crafters.|n• Gather while you do world quests and delves.|n• Collect map |cffffff00treasures|r (addon Professions tab shows pins).|n• Spend KP into nodes that give |cffffff00more herbs per node|r or |cffffff00faster gathering|r.|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP|r|n|n• Pick one zone or herb type you farm most.|n• Depletion and speed nodes are strong for beginners.|n|n|cffffcc00Gold|r|nSell raw herbs on the AH when prices are high (often raid release week). Even without Alchemy, herbs alone can make gold.|n|n|cffffcc00Works with|r|nSend herbs to your Alchemist via |cffffff00Warband bank|r.",

	PROFGUIDE_SEC_SKINNING_TITLE = "Skinning",
	PROFGUIDE_SEC_SKINNING_BODY = "|cffffcc00What it does|r|nYou |cffffff00skin beasts|r for leather. Leather feeds |cffffff00Leatherworking|r.|n|n|cffffcc00Who should learn it?|r|n|n• Pairs with |cffffff00Leatherworking|r (same char or alt).|n• Great while leveling — kill mobs, skin them.|n|n|cffffcc00Week 1 checklist|r|n|n• Learn Skinning.|n• Skin every beast you kill in delves and open world.|n• Map treasures via Professions tab.|n• KP: more leather per skin and faster gathering.|n|n|cffffcc00Gold|r|nSell leather stacks on the AH, or craft with Leatherworking for higher profit.|n|n|cffffcc00Tip|r|nYou do not need a crafting station to skin — only a skinning knife in your bags.",

	PROFGUIDE_SEC_LEATHERWORKING_TITLE = "Leatherworking",
	PROFGUIDE_SEC_LEATHERWORKING_BODY = "|cffffcc00What it does|r|nTurns leather into |cffffff00leather armor|r and gear for leather users (Druids, Monks, Rogues, etc.).|n|n|cffffcc00Good combo|r|n|cffffff00Skinning|r on the same character or a gather-alt.|n|n|cffffcc00Week 1 checklist|r|n|n• Learn Leatherworking.|n• First-craft cheap recipes.|n• Weekly quest + Patron Orders.|n• Choose armor type: |cffffff00leather|r vs |cffffff00mail|r paths in specs (pick what you wear or what sells).|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP — for yourself|r|n|n• Craft gear upgrades for your |cffffff00own slots|r as you level.|n|n|cffffcc00Where to spend KP — for gold|r|n|n• Endgame |cffffff00crafted leather pieces|r can sell to players replacing gear.|n• Check which slots are weak on the AH before you specialize.|n|n|cffffcc00Crafting orders|r|nPublic orders for popular leather items appear in Silvermoon — good once your quality is high enough.",

